# OpenTDF TDF3 for Swift

Experimental SwiftPM library product/module `OpenTDFTDF3`, built from shared Go
source with Goalchemy. Requires Swift 6.4.0, a C compiler, pkg-config, OpenSSL 3,
zlib and libcurl development packages. Linux x86_64 is the verified baseline;
macOS and iOS integration have not been verified.

Add this directory as a SwiftPM dependency and depend on its `OpenTDFTDF3`
product. The module exports the OpenTDF handle API: `SDK(endpoint, Options(...))`
creates a client; `sdk.encryptBytes(data, TDFOptions(...))` and
`sdk.decryptBytes(data, ReaderOptions(...))` move payloads as `Data`;
`createTDF` and `loadTDF` return `TDFObject` and `Reader` handles for the
manifest, policy, attributes and unencrypted metadata; `sdk.attributes` and the
other service clients take and return the SwiftProtobuf platform messages.
Methods are `async throws` and honour Task cancellation.

Strings are Swift `String`s, sizes `Int64`, and every unset option is the
reference default. `Options.tokenProvider` takes a `TokenProvider` closure that
resolves an `AccessToken` and replaces client credentials. Failures throw
`OpenTDFError` with a stable `kind`, the reference's message, HTTP status and
service fields. No Go runtime is invoked. Goalchemy's runtime license is
included in `LICENSE`.
